      "created_at": "2013-03-30T21:05:31.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"GreaserMedic\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/greasermedic/48/2080_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> GreaserMedic:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks for the reply, I really appreciate it escpecially because this topic probably comes up at least once a month. &nbsp;My problem is with the 1-2 mm wider Rook City cards that do not fit into 64 mm wide sleeves I have been using for EE. &nbsp;I have seen topics on BGG alking about the size discrepancy but no solution was listed. &nbsp;For someone who obsessively sleeves, the whole thing is really irritating…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I sort of barely made them fit the Green May days I was using. The height was fine, but width was off too.</p>\n<p>ST and IR fits perfectly though. (SInce my EE was also the taller ones, but protects majority of the cards.)<br>&nbsp;</p>",
